<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίμᾰχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that may easily be
			attacked</i>, <i>assailable</i>, of fortified places, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμαχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῆς γῆς ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.31
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				35
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -ώτατα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ τὸ -ώτατον ἦν τοῦ χωρίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.21
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				6.133
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>.
				<i>contended for, contested</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				8.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>.
				<i>equipped for battle</i>, Thom.Mag.<i><span class="en">
				p.113R.
			</span></i>; epith. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλούτων</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				3520
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cnidus</span>), cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1014.61
			</span></i> (Erythrae, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>. <i>ally, helper</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.659
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. χωρία</span>
			<i>impregnable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.383
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπο-</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
